WEBVTT

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.890
<i>Huh? I...</i>

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.200
<i>From Kento?</i>

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.870
<i>I'm at Pluto's Sheep.</i>

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:10.050
<i>Let's talk.</i>

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.170
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.350
<i>Talk about what?</i>

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:23.730
<i>Again...</i>

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:42.170
<i>I wonder what he wants to talk about.</i>

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.400
<i>He kind of looks angry.</i>

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:54.030
I'm not a mind reader.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.590
I won't understand if you don't tell me.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:02.150
I understand that you object to my attitude toward you.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.500
However, if that's the case, you must make yourself clear.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.500
<i>What is he talking about?</i>

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.020
With regards to courting women,

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:15.460
I've tried to only act according to what I researched.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.470
<i>Courting?</i>

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:21.170
If there is something that I'm missing, I'll try to take care of it.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:24.890
But first, I need you to tell me what you're dissatisfied with.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:27.420
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.350
Are you listening?

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.270
How about saying something?

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.450
I'm sorry. I... don't really understand.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.950
Why are you apologizing?

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:43.200
Don't tell me you suddenly felt like apologizing for no reason.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.870
That can't happen.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.770
Um...

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.330
To think that you'd apologize to me.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:55.550
There are still mountains of unanswered riddles in the world.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.050
Well, how do I say this?

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.220
I'm sorry, too.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.010
Huh?

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:07.360
I was unaware of your displeasure and said something immature.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.580
I'm sorry.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:10.690
It's fine...

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.880
<i>I guess it worked out somehow,</i>

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:16.930
<i>but I have no idea what he's talking about.</i>

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.830
Shall we walk a bit?

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:21.570
Yes.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.890
Is something wrong?

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.720
I'm a little tired.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:51.030
Um, where are we walking to?

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:55.970
When I asked my friend what a girl and guy who just started dating should do,

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:59.440
he told me to walk aimlessly by the train station.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.110
<i>Is this supposed to be a date?</i>

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.370
But what's the point of this?

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.500
<i>Like I thought.</i>

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.080
<i>This is another world.</i>

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.380
<i>The world that you're currently in might not be the same world as the original,</i>

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.840
<i>but the truth is, this might be the real world.</i>

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.720
<i>You appear to be in a very unstable situation.</i>

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:37.470
<i>I've received texts from Kento every day,</i>

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.190
<i>but it's only ever "good morning" or "good night."</i>

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:47.980
<i>Tomorrow, I'll be in the university lab all day.</i>

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.970
<i>Come by if you're not busy.</i>

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:00.470
Just sit wherever.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.750
There are drinks in the fridge.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.340
Help yourself.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.340
Okay.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:24.540
<i>He's a graduate student in mathematics.</i>

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:29.660
<i>I wonder what kind of research he's doing.</i>

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.040
<i>Was there some reason he asked me to come here?</i>

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:49.040
<i>Maybe I should say something.</i>

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:58.230
<i>Or maybe I shouldn't interrupt him.</i>

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:13.690
U-Um, there was something you wanted, right?

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.080
Wanted? What do you mean?

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:19.580
What?

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:23.480
You're the one who said you wanted to spend more time together before.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:28.110
That's why I decided to spend today with you.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:33.820
However, I had work, so I had you come here.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.220
Um...

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.740
Is there a problem?

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:41.520
I-I kind of wanted to talk a little.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.480
I'll listen.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.280
<i>But what do I say?</i>

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:59.010
With regards to male-female communication in dating,

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:03.170
I heard that this sort of act is especially effective.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:05.960
Um...

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.090
Sorry. It kind of hurts.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:12.880
Sorry.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.350
I don't know how much strength I should use.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:21.100
I have no clue how much pressure I should apply with my fingers.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.680
I should've looked into that as well.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.740
Well, to your stations.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:46.500
<i>This Waka doesn't talk much.</i>

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.330
Hey!

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.470
So, you're wearing a yukata today?

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:54.020
You're going to the temple festival with Kento, right?

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:56.560
Oh, that's right.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.340
Yes, I plan on wearing one.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:01.380
You were really excited about it, after all!

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:03.250
That's right.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:12.140
<i>There was a text about today, but...</i>

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.970
<i>We promised to meet, right?</i>

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:21.450
<i>He's not coming.</i>

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.520
<i>Did I get the time wrong?</i>

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:27.310
<i>Nope.</i>

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.730
<i>What time do you get off work?</i>

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:45.040
<i>I'm already off work.</i>

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.440
<i>We planned on going to the temple festival,</i>

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.860
<i>so I'm at the station where we were going to meet.</i>

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:00.460
Yes, hello?

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:03.380
I'm sorry! That's right.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:06.500
We promised we'd go to the temple festival today.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.460
It was an event I had absolutely no interest in,

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.650
so I completely forgot about it.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:17.350
Even if I head over now, you'll have to wait.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.080
Don't worry about it.

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:21.220
Maybe another time...

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:21.940
No, no.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:23.540
I'm coming right now.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:24.620
Wait there.

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:37.840
Sorry to make you wait.

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:39.530
Are you okay?

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:40.670
Yeah.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.590
You came in a yukata on a cold day like this?

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:47.970
Yes.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:53.160
Did you do that just for me?

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:59.440
No, to think you'd do that for me is incredibly conceited of me.

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:00.290
Let's go.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:18.880
<i>Kento has memories of spending time with me that I don't have.</i>

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.300
<i>If I keep pretending like nothing's wrong,</i>

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:25.760
<i>I...</i>

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:38.080
It sure is busy despite the rain.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:38.840
Yeah.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.000
Be careful we don't get separated.

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:45.120
If you're not against it...

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:49.390
It'd be helpful if you held the umbrella too.

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:54.150
So we don't get separated in the crowd.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.280
No other reason.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:12:00.600
And only if you're not against it.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.450
If that's the case, I'll think of a different method.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.700
I see.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:13.050
That's just fine.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:27.690
You told me to promise you just one thing.

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:32.640
Promise?

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:37.890
We promised to come to the temple festival when we first started going out.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:42.720
Even though I couldn't possibly imagine myself going on a date,

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:47.510
you told me to promise just one thing and told me about this temple festival.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:49.970
<i>So that's how it happened.</i>

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:56.970
I didn't notice when, but it stopped raining.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.780
I'm sorry about today.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.950
I had no interest in temple festivals,

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:20.780
so I had completely forgotten about our promise, but... well...

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:25.150
Once I was here, I found that it was surprisingly fun.

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:27.040
I'm glad.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.700
I first thought that dating you would be impossible,

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.810
but it also turned out to be unexpectedly fun.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.010
How strange.

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.540
I had fun too.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.260
Thank you very much.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.770
Is something wrong?

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:49.780
Nothing. You're just so upfront.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.090
Mandarin.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:11.630
You brought me mocha before.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:13.470
Yeah.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:15.890
I thought so.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:25.440
Today's the first day you've brought me coffee.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:30.740
So, I have something that I'd like to ask you.

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:37.080
For the past few weeks,

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:40.550
you've been acting quite differently than before.

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:45.140
I analyzed possible explanations in my own way.

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:48.380
From the typical mood swings afflicting most women

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:50.340
to an alien abduction.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:53.220
I came up with a number of hypotheses.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:59.690
And then, after eliminating all other possibilities,

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:02.690
only one remained.

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:05.730
I'll tell you my conclusion.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:10.110
You are missing your memories.

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:15.610
I'm still investigating as to what extent.

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:24.330
Or at the least, it's very likely that you've forgotten everything that's happened since we started going out.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:27.230
Well? Do you have any objections?

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.960
I think it's okay to tell him.

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.410
Orion!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.820
What is it?

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.530
Um...

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:40.490
Well...

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.380
Is there something there?

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:45.470
Um...

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:51.710
I only saw a little bit of your interaction, but I think Kento will understand.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:56.990
I see.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.530
I understand the gist of it.

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.440
He understands?

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:07.840
When a scientist sees fireworks,

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:11.730
he thinks about the chemical reactions and doesn't appreciate the beauty.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:13.510
At least that's what the layman believes.

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:15.600
But that's not true at all.

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:19.800
In mathematics, there are situations where even romance is necessary.

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:26.540
As for the current problem, let's say that a fairy has attached itself to you.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.760
Don't talk like I'm an evil spirit!

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:32.580
What sort of shape or form does the fairy take?

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:34.570
Don't talk like I'm an object!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:40.490
He's like a normal boy, but he has things like horns on his head,

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:41.920
and his clothes are a little strange...

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:44.030
Don't talk like I'm a weirdo!

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.090
Draw me a picture.

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.120
Um...

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:56.250
What is this? It's totally wrong!

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:57.900
I'm sorry.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:59.810
I couldn't draw him very well.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:04.040
Only you can see him, and he has no physical form,

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:06.510
so he can't interact with the world.

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:09.740
So he's just floating there.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:10.390
Yes.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:12.750
Now I feel like I'm being treated like I'm useless.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:17.090
Well, I'd like to talk to him. Is that okay?

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.660
He wants to talk with me?

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:21.900
That's fine, but how?

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:23.990
He says it's fine.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:27.610
Then I'd like to record what the fairy says,

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:30.010
so could you transcribe his words?

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:30.830
Okay.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:34.060
Man, I'm nervous!

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:36.190
Uh, nice to meet you.

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:37.820
I'm Orion.

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:42.510
He doesn't appear to be very intelligent.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.190
Hey!

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:46.940
What do you mean? That was a normal introduction!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.520
What's he saying?

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.480
He's a little upset.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:54.530
An exceedingly human response.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:57.560
In that case, I'll treat him as a human.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.960
Nice to meet you, fairy.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:05.570
Am I the first person aside from her who has introduced himself to you?

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:08.490
That's right. It's really surprising!

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:11.320
"Surprising," huh?

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.630
He appears to be a bright and cheerful fairy.

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:16.750
Basically,

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:21.560
this fairy exists in a different world from ours?

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:22.880
That's right.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:24.630
You're quick to catch on.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:28.710
And he said that things have become complicated?

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.600
Specifically, what does that mean?

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:36.390
I wasn't able to contact her very well for a while.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.310
How did that happen?

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:41.190
The reason isn't clear,

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:45.940
but she moved into a world different from the world she was originally in,

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:48.950
and she's been shifting around since then.

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:50.730
What do you mean?

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.250
There's no difference with her,

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:57.710
but she keeps being sent off into new worlds where her surroundings are slightly different.

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:04.470
So parallel worlds exist, and she's moving between them?

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:14.640
If that assumption is true, then she's not the girl that I know?

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:16.920
I'm not sure.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:20.060
Now I understand.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.820
The reason your attitude changed

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:30.260
wasn't because you began to emotionally invest in me little by little as I had initially thought.

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:37.580
So there's a possibility that she might shift to a new world again?

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:40.750
Yes, she might.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.850
He seems sad.

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:53.380
He believed our story and listened with his full attention.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:54.260
Yeah.

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:56.680
But I wonder if we've wronged Kento somehow.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:01.180
But I think that the you in this world...

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:04.230
Did something happen?

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:05.570
He disappeared.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:06.950
I see.

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:09.860
I wanted to ask him more questions.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:16.170
The you and me from before would always fight when we met.

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:21.390
You were always displeased with something about me.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:24.090
You wanted me to consider human emotions more.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:28.730
I have often hurt people with my arguments.

00:20:29.780 --> 00:20:32.260
I'm sure that was the cause of our quarrels.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:38.920
However, argument and logic are not always the right path to take.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:42.450
Honestly expressing emotions is important.

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:46.140
You were the one who helped me realize that.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:48.570
Thank you.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:01.590
Kento.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:09.030
I think the me from this world just wasn't able to be honest with you and really did like you.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.440
I wonder.

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:12.300
Yes, I'm sure of it.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:20.520
I hope I can honestly open myself up to you again.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.760
Will I be able to see you tomorrow?

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:33.210
Yes.

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:54.690
What are you spacing out for?

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:30.790
Did you see how many bottles of water Kento had in his lab?

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:33.260
There were a number of different brands,

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:35.500
but I wonder if they all really taste different.

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:40.250
I can't drink, so taste and compare them for me sometime.
